{
  "requirement": "Saved configuration MUST remain distinct from resolved runtime configuration.\nSerializing and deserializing a valid configuration MUST preserve its semantic\nvalues, including explicit versus omitted settings. Optional fields MAY be\nomitted on serialization; defaults and environment-derived values MUST NOT be\nmaterialized into omitted fields. TOML comments and formatting need not\nround-trip.\n\nLoading configuration or running a configured feature MUST NOT rewrite the user\nor project configuration as a side effect. Resolved credentials and live runtime\nobjects MUST NOT enter the serialized data structures. Explicitly supplied\ncredential values are permitted only in the fields documented by the authoring\nfeature; credentials resolved from a profile or environment MUST NOT be written\nback to configuration.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: the sources satisfy `requirements.configuration.serialization`.**\n\n**Saved configuration is distinct from resolved runtime configuration**\n- The saved types (`UserConfig`, `WorkspaceConfig`, `AuthoringConfig`, `BackendConfig`, and related types in `src/config.rs`) derive `Serialize` and `Deserialize`.\n- `ResolvedAuthoringConfig` is a separate type. It does not derive `Serialize`, and it carries only the selected saved values and their source (`resolve_authoring_with_workspace_from`, lines 843–924).\n- The only credentials it can hold are values the user explicitly supplied.\n\n**Round trip preserves semantic values, and omitted settings stay omitted**\n- Optional fields use `#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]`. Empty maps and vectors use the corresponding `is_empty` skip.\n- `UserConfig::to_toml` and `WorkspaceConfig::to_toml` (lines 224–230 and 260–272) validate the config and then serialize it. Neither adds defaults.\n- `OllamaConfig::endpoint()` applies its default at read time rather than writing it into the struct.\n- `concurrency` is `None` unless the user set it, and `effective_concurrency` is computed in the resolved type.\n- `OptionValue` is untagged, so integers and floats round-trip. Non-finite floats are rejected.\n- Collapsing an explicit empty `options = {}` or `projects = {}` into an omitted field is the same semantic value, so I do not treat it as a defect.\n\n**Loading and running do not rewrite configuration**\n- `load_user_config`, `load_workspace_config`, `UserConfig::parse`, `WorkspaceConfig::parse` and the resolve functions only read.\n- I found no write to user or workspace configuration anywhere in `src/`.\n- `src/setup.rs` edits `book.toml`, but only through the explicit `habeas setup` command, which is a separate requirement (`requirements.cli.setup`).\n\n**Resolved credentials stay out of serialized data**\n- `OllamaConfig::api_key_from` (lines 522–539) returns an owned `String` read from the environment. It does not store that value in the struct.\n- Bedrock credentials come from the AWS SDK chain, and `bedrock_sdk_config` (in `src/authoring/providers.rs`) does not write them back.\n- Explicit `credentials` and `api_key` values are serialized, and only in their documented fields.\n- `SecretString` redacts itself in `Debug`.\n\n**Tests in `tests/configuration.rs` cover the main points**\n- `absent_and_minimal_configuration_are_distinct_and_read_only` (line 70) checks that an absent file stays absent, that the file contents (comment included) are unchanged after loading, and that the config round-trips.\n- `backend_configuration_round_trips_without_materializing_defaults` (line 104) checks that serializing a config with no `endpoint` or `concurrency` does not add them. It also checks that nested options, floats, integers, booleans and arrays survive the round trip.\n- `authoring_concurrency_defaults_overrides_and_invalid_values` (line 156) checks that the effective concurrency default is not serialized, that an explicit `concurrency = 7` is, and that it round-trips.\n- `ollama_authentication_resolves_separately_and_rejects_missing_values` (line 297) checks that `api_key_env` is serialized but the environment value (\"private-value\") is not.\n- `workspace_discovery_uses_nearest_file_without_merging_or_rewriting_it` (line 328) checks that the file is unchanged after loading and that the workspace config round-trips.\n- `workspace_defaults_and_configs_combine_with_existing_user_selections` (line 424) checks that resolving configs with both a user and a workspace file keeps the saved values and their source separate.\n- `explicit_credentials_round_trip_but_diagnostics_and_debug_redact_them` (line 530) checks that explicit credentials round-trip and that `Debug` output and error messages redact them.\n\n**Marking**\n- The `to_toml`, `parse`, load, resolve and `api_key` functions all carry `{impl}` markers for this requirement.\n- The `skip_serializing_if` attributes that implement omission sit on the struct definitions, which have no `{impl}` marker of their own. The marked `to_toml` functions cover them.\n- `resolve_authoring` (line 807) is not marked for this requirement. It only composes marked functions, so this is a minor omission and not a gap in behavior.\n\nI found no unspecified behavior in the marked code. The remaining checks (version, name and credential validation) are tied to other requirements.",
